      "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith the SHUFFLE 5D KV layout (`SGLANG_AITER_KV_CACHE_LAYOUT=vectorized_5d`), `AiterAttnBackend` still allocates the `paged_attention_ragged` workspace although decode runs through `pa_decode_gluon`, wasting `max_bs * num_heads * ceil(context_len / 256) * (head_dim + 2) * 4` bytes of HBM; this PR skips the allocation whenever decode does not use `paged_attention_ragged`.\n\nThe allocation guard checks only `use_mla` and `use_triton_unified_attention`, while `forward_decode` sends 5D pools to `forward_decode_vectorized_5d` before reaching the buffer's only reader. #47042 already uses the full predicate (MLA, unified attention or 5D) for the partition buckets.\n\nUnused workspace at `max_bs = 4096`, TP1:\n\n| Model | context | unused workspace |\n|---|---|---|\n| Qwen3-8B | 40960 | 10.2 GiB |\n| Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct | 131072 | 32.5 GiB |\n| MiniMax-M2.7 | 204800 | 76.2 GiB |\n\nOn MI355X at `main@f85ca901e2`, MiniMax-M2.7 at TP1 with the 5D layout fails at startup with `torch.OutOfMemoryError: ... Tried to allocate 76.17 GiB`; with this change it starts and decodes.\n\nOnly plain MHA pools with the opt-in 5D layout reach this code; the default NHD layout is unchanged. MLA and sliding-window models already skip the allocation, and hybrid linear-attention pools never report the 5D layout.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Add `AiterAttnBackend._uses_paged_ragged_decode()`, the predicate `_build_decode_partition_buckets` computed inline, and use it for the `workspace_buffer` allocation too.\n- Add a CPU test to `test_aiter_verify_metadata.py` that builds the backend on a plain MHA pool and checks the workspace is allocated for NHD and skipped for `vectorized_5d`. It fails on main, on a variant that never allocates the workspace, and on one that keys the guard on the env var instead of the pool's layout.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable: the skipped buffer is never read on the 5D path, and the NHD path allocates the same buffer as before.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nOnly an init-time allocation is removed; no per-step change is expected. Serving numbers on current main: TBD.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n---\n\nFound by [Hyperloom](https://github.com/AMD-AGI/Hyperloom); reviewed and measured by hand.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #41427825312](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41427825312)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41427825205](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41427825205)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41427825290](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41427825290)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
